WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.741 --> 00:00:01.600
- What up internet?

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.396
My name is Nancy and
today I'm gonna be walking

00:00:03.396 --> 00:00:05.111
around the BuzzFeed office
trying to see if my coworkers

00:00:05.111 --> 00:00:07.528
know how to say my last name.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:12.822
How long have we been friends?

00:00:12.822 --> 00:00:13.665
- Almost a year?

00:00:13.665 --> 00:00:14.900
- A little over a year.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.540
- For a good half a year.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.365
- Would you say that we're good friends?

00:00:18.365 --> 00:00:19.198
- Yeah.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.654
- Yeah, we're good friends, we hang.

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:21.908
- I've been to your house.

00:00:21.908 --> 00:00:23.265
- Do you know how to
pronounce my last name?

00:00:23.265 --> 00:00:26.015
(record scratch)

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.360
- Oh, no no no no no, I can't do it.

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:30.899
- Noy-wen.

00:00:31.838 --> 00:00:32.671
- Ehhh...

00:00:32.671 --> 00:00:33.504
No.

00:00:33.504 --> 00:00:36.547
- I don't want to try 'cause I feel like

00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:37.868
I'm gonna mess it up.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:38.987
- It's Noo-yin?

00:00:38.987 --> 00:00:42.194
I had a friend in high
school named Julian Noo-yin.

00:00:42.194 --> 00:00:43.111
- It's not.

00:00:43.124 --> 00:00:43.957
- Waynge?

00:00:44.747 --> 00:00:45.580
- No.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.448
- It's Noo-wen?

00:00:46.448 --> 00:00:47.977
- It's still wrong.

00:00:47.977 --> 00:00:49.649
- I feel like I just blew your mind.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:53.251
- I've been saying Noy-wen
since middle school.

00:00:53.251 --> 00:00:54.084
- N'wen.

00:00:54.808 --> 00:00:55.891
- Alright I'll take that.

00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:56.724
- Wen?

00:00:57.707 --> 00:00:58.540
Hmmm?

00:00:58.993 --> 00:01:00.222
- It's actually Wheng.

00:01:00.222 --> 00:01:01.305
- Wang. Wang?

00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:02.849
Wheng.

00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:04.579
- Oh, I don't want to try again.

00:01:04.579 --> 00:01:05.412
- Wheng.

00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:06.967
- Wang.

00:01:07.742 --> 00:01:08.575
Everybody always says Wang.

00:01:08.575 --> 00:01:09.492
It's Wheng.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.882
- What? Can you come
closer and say that again?

00:01:11.882 --> 00:01:12.715
- Wheng.

00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:13.548
- Wayne?

00:01:14.118 --> 00:01:15.426
- You're just saying Wayne now.

00:01:15.426 --> 00:01:16.604
- I wanna crawl into
your mouth and figure out

00:01:16.604 --> 00:01:18.683
where you're holding the word.

00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:19.516
- Wheng.

00:01:19.689 --> 00:01:20.522
- Whang?

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:22.142
- That's actually good.

00:01:22.142 --> 00:01:23.572
- So the thing about
the Vietnamese language,

00:01:23.572 --> 00:01:25.503
is that it's a monosyllabic language,

00:01:25.503 --> 00:01:27.802
so every single word is only one syllable.

00:01:27.802 --> 00:01:31.885
So Nguyen is one word, so
Noy-wen is not correct.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:35.375
A lot of the sounds that
goes into my last name,

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:37.437
doesn't really exist in
the English language.

00:01:37.437 --> 00:01:40.045
- Nancy told me how to pronounce
her last name last year,

00:01:40.045 --> 00:01:43.212
and my dentist has the same last name,

00:01:43.488 --> 00:01:46.007
so I was able to call her doctor Wheng,

00:01:46.007 --> 00:01:47.998
and I could tell it meant a lot to her

00:01:47.998 --> 00:01:50.164
that I said her last name correctly.

00:01:50.164 --> 00:01:51.192
Thank you, Nancy.

00:01:51.192 --> 00:01:54.075
- I've heard my last name
butchered in so many different

00:01:54.075 --> 00:01:55.962
ways that nothing really
phases me anymore.

00:01:55.962 --> 00:01:58.045
We're all learning today.

00:01:59.592 --> 00:02:04.259
Not really me, but definitely
a lot of other people are.

00:02:05.317 --> 00:02:06.571
("Blue Danube")

00:02:06.571 --> 00:02:08.437
- I'm really sorry, Nancy.

00:02:08.437 --> 00:02:09.585
(laughing)

00:02:09.585 --> 00:02:11.477
- It's okay, we're still good friends.

00:02:11.477 --> 00:02:12.532
You want a hug?

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.782
- [friend] Yes.

